/-!
# Source-paid pair-Duhamel quantum cascade

The occurrence-level source quantum is now accumulated without asking a
caller to choose the visible branch.  At each reduced-core node the source
itself writes the positive pair-Duhamel rate quantum when that quantum enters
an actual visible row.  If no such visible witness exists, the scalar payment
coordinate is zero while the producer retains its exact annular or native
pair/gluing responsibility.

Strict absolute occurrences inject every positive paid quantum into the
authoritative whole-run exact-causal prefix.  This is consume-before-quotient:
the scalar coordinate records only physical visible payment, while pair
kernel and gluing cancellation continue through their native carriers.
-/

